>> title: Margherita
>> category: Pizzas
>> tags: pizza, tomato, mozzarella, basil, italian, oven
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: pizza margherita, margarita, margarita pizza, marg, cheese pizza, cheese pie, plain slice, a regular, Neapolitan pizza
>> pairs-with: pizza-dough, basil-pesto
>> servings: 2
>> time: 1 hr
>> step.2: crush by hand, and do not cook it
>> step.3: stretch to 12 in, thick at the rim
>> step.4: top thin, cheese in the gaps
>> step.5: bake 550°F (290°C) 6 to 8 min
>> step.6: finish with oil, off the heat

Preheat a #baking steel{} on the upper rack of the #oven{} at 550°F (290°C) ~preheat{45%min}, as hot as it will go.

Crush @whole peeled tomatoes{14%oz}(400 g; San Marzano, drained of the thin juice) by hand with @fine sea salt{1/2%tsp} and @extra-virgin olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL). Raw, and it stays raw — it cooks in the eight minutes the pie is in the oven, which is the difference between a pizza and a plate of stewed tomato.

Stretch @pizza dough{2%balls}(250 g each; from the recipe on this shelf) out to 12 in on @semolina{2%Tbs}(20 g), pressing the middle thin and leaving a half-inch rim untouched.

Top @&(~1)stretched dough{} with @&(~2)crushed tomato{} spread thin to the rim, then @fresh mozzarella{8%oz}(225 g; torn, drained an hour on a rack) dropped in gaps rather than laid over, and @fresh basil{10%leaves} tucked under the cheese so it steams instead of burning.

Bake @&(~1)dressed pie{} on the steel ~bake{7%min}, until the rim has puffed and spotted and the underside lifts stiff off the peel.

Finish @&(~1)pizza{} with @olive oil{2%tsp}(10 mL) poured over in a thread, and cut it within the minute.

Bake it hotter than feels reasonable for less time than feels safe. This is a 550°F home oven on a steel, not the 800°F deck that gives a Neapolitan pie its ninety-second leopard spotting, and the crust it makes is drier and crisper rather than soft and foldable — a good pie, and an honestly different one. Two balls of dough are left from the recipe this leans on, which is what a dough that keeps four days in the fridge is for.
